[node name="RichTextLabel" type="RichTextLabel" parent="DockTabContainer/HelpTab/GettingStarted/VBoxContainer/SetupHelp" unique_id=1514331880]
visible = false
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(560, 0)
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
size_flags_vertical = 3
theme_override_styles/normal = SubResource("StyleBoxEmpty_2vjd2")
theme_override_styles/focus = SubResource("StyleBoxEmpty_2vjd2")
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "GDLogger works immediately with the default configuration and comes with a single \"general\" category. Meaning you can instantly start creating entries such as: 
    [i][color=#dcdcaa]Log[/color].[color=#6dc2ff]msg[/color]([color=#ce9178]\"This is my first log entry.\"[/color], [color=#ce9178]\"game\"[/color])[/i]

Use the Logs tab to add, remove, or rename categories and even read log files. Sessions dictate when the plugin logs entries or not, which automatically starts at runtime by default. But this can be turned off in the settings.

GDLogger uses an [b]Log[/b] singleton, making its functions accessible from all scenes and scripts.

[b]Note[/b] that autloaded scenes and scripts are loaded in the order of the list in your ProjectSettings. If another autoload is trying to log an entry before Log, the entry may bot be logged. Move Log higher in the list to fix this.
	"
fit_content = true

[node name="CategoriesHelp" type="FoldableContainer" parent="DockTabContainer/HelpTab/GettingStarted/VBoxContainer" unique_id=1969559512]
unique_name_in_owner = true
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
theme = ExtResource("4_o07th")
folded = true
title = "Categories"
foldable_group = SubResource("FoldableGroup_tvbkj")

[node name="RichTextLabel" type="RichTextLabel" parent="DockTabContainer/HelpTab/GettingStarted/VBoxContainer/CategoriesHelp" unique_id=165372222]
visible = false
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(560, 0)
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
size_flags_vertical = 3
theme_override_styles/normal = SubResource("StyleBoxEmpty_2vjd2")
theme_override_styles/focus = SubResource("StyleBoxEmpty_2vjd2")
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "Every category creates it's own logs at the start of each session in their respective directory within your base directory. This allows you to sort your log entries into separate files to make them more manageable and legible. But you can still use one singular category if that's preferred.

Additionally, within the dock, you can mark one of your categories as 'Default'. Logging entries without specifying a category will log it to the marked default category. This is especially useful if you have one overarching category for general entries. Or in case you only use a single category to log and don't necessitates you to specify the category constantly.

The Left/Right arrows allows you to sort the order of the categories in the dock but this has no effect on your logs and is purely visual.  

The Open Folder button will load that category's log files for you to open and read."
fit_content = true

[node name="LogBrowserHelp" type="FoldableContainer" parent="DockTabContainer/HelpTab/GettingStarted/VBoxContainer" unique_id=76721491]
unique_name_in_owner = true
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
theme = ExtResource("4_o07th")
folded = true
title = "Log Browser"
foldable_group = SubResource("FoldableGroup_tvbkj")

[node name="RichTextLabel" type="RichTextLabel" parent="DockTabContainer/HelpTab/GettingStarted/VBoxContainer/LogBrowserHelp" unique_id=1476901840]
visible = false
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(560, 0)
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
size_flags_vertical = 3
theme_override_styles/normal = SubResource("StyleBoxEmpty_2vjd2")
theme_override_styles/focus = SubResource("StyleBoxEmpty_2vjd2")
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "A new feature in 2.0 allows you to browse and read .log files all within the editor. You can select a log file to read your file and in the top right of the popup, the settings button allows you to customize the look of the font, size, color etc. 
Alternatively, you can also use the settings button in the Logs tag affords you additional customization.

Loading large files for viewing may freeze Godot depending on the file size and your computer's performance. If this is affecting you, lower your Entry Count or Session Timer settings. You can also enable the option to open with OS which will be faster.

Future updates may include:
	Proper folder navigation
	File renaming
	File deletion
"
fit_content = true

[node name="MessagesHelp" type="FoldableContainer" parent="DockTabContainer/HelpTab/GettingStarted/VBoxContainer" unique_id=487613138]
unique_name_in_owner = true
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
theme = ExtResource("4_o07th")
folded = true
title = "Messages / Entries"
foldable_group = SubResource("FoldableGroup_tvbkj")

[node name="RichTextLabel" type="RichTextLabel" parent="DockTabContainer/HelpTab/GettingStarted/VBoxContainer/MessagesHelp" unique_id=1166564036]
visible = false
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(560, 0)
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
size_flags_vertical = 3
theme_override_styles/normal = SubResource("StyleBoxEmpty_2vjd2")
theme_override_styles/focus = SubResource("StyleBoxEmpty_2vjd2")
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "Messages(msg) or entries are plain text strings and can include any data that can be converted to a string, allowing flexible and descriptive logging. 

[i][color=#57b3ff]Log[/color].[color=#63c5da]msg[/color]([color=#b8b8b8]log_msg[/color] [color=#ff7085]:[/color] [color=#42ffc2]String[/color], [color=#b8b8b8]category_name[/color][color=#ff7085]:[/color] [color=#42ffc2]String[/color] [color=#ff7085]=[/color] [color=#ffeca1]\"\"[/color], [color=#b8b8b8]print_msg[/color][color=#ff7085]:[/color] [color=#42ffc2]bool[/color] [color=#ff7085]=[/color] [color=#ff7085]false[/color])[/i]

The [b][color=#57b3ff]Log[/color].[color=#63c5da]msg[/color]()[/b] function requires only a string or message/entry to be passed in but has additional arguments you can pass in, such as the category you want the entry to be logged into(is required if you haven't marked one of your categories as [i]default[/i]. 

You can also use [i]print_msg[/i] to print individual entries if desired. 

[b]Example:[/b]
    [color=#ff7085]func[/color] [color=#6dc2ff]_on_damage_taken[/color]([color=#c586c0]amount[/color]: [color=#4ec9b0]float[/color], [color=#c586c0]source[/color]: [color=#4ec9b0]CharacterBody2D[/color])  ->  [color=#4ec9b0]void[/color]:
        [color=#c586c0]current_health[/color] -= [color=#c586c0]amount[/color]
        [color=#dcdcaa]Log[/color].[color=#6dc2ff]msg[/color]([color=#ce9178]\"Player took \"[/color] + [color=#dcdcaa]str[/color]([color=#c586c0]amount[/color]) + [color=#ce9178]\" damage from entity [\"[/color] + [color=#c586c0]source[/color].[color=#6dc2ff]get_name[/color]() + [color=#ce9178]\"] - Current health: \"[/color] + [color=#dcdcaa]str[/color]([color=#c586c0]current_health[/color]) + [color=#ce9178]\" / \"[/color] + [color=#dcdcaa]str[/color]([color=#c586c0]max_health[/color]))
        [color=#6a9955]# Player took 16.4 damage from entity [GoblinA] - Current health: 139.96 / 268[/color]
    "
fit_content = true

[node name="DirectoryHelp" type="FoldableContainer" parent="DockTabContainer/HelpTab/GettingStarted/VBoxContainer" unique_id=694307931]
unique_name_in_owner = true
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
theme = ExtResource("4_o07th")
folded = true
title = "Directories"
foldable_group = SubResource("FoldableGroup_tvbkj")

[node name="RichTextLabel" type="RichTextLabel" parent="DockTabContainer/HelpTab/GettingStarted/VBoxContainer/DirectoryHelp" unique_id=1565100639]
visible = false
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(560, 0)
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
size_flags_vertical = 3
theme_override_styles/normal = SubResource("StyleBoxEmpty_2vjd2")
theme_override_styles/focus = SubResource("StyleBoxEmpty_2vjd2")
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "The default directory where your [color=#ffeca1].log[/color] files are stored is [color=#ffeca1]\"user://gdlogger/\"[/color]. Since this directory is outside of the [color=#ffeca1]\"res://\"[/color] (project folder), it isn't packaged with your project when you export it, meaning your users/players have access to the files and can share them with the developer. It is recommended that you use [color=#ffeca1]\"user://\"[/color] but change the [color=#ffeca1]\"gdlogger\"[/color] part.

[color=lightred][b]Warning![/b][/color] [color=pink]Do [b]NOT[/b] use [color=#ffeca1]\"user://logs/\"[/color]. Godot stores its own logs in that folder and you risk that GDLogger might delete said logs in its operations. There are safeguards to prevent this directory from being used but still, never use it.[/color]

Remember that there are buttons to open the directory using your operating system's file browser. You can also use the normal Project > [color=#ffeca1]\"Open User Data Folder\"[/color] in Godot.
"
fit_content = true

[node name="ConcurrenciesHelp" type="FoldableContainer" parent="DockTabContainer/HelpTab/GettingStarted/VBoxContainer" unique_id=665020188]
unique_name_in_owner = true
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
theme = ExtResource("4_o07th")
folded = true
title = "Multiple Instances"
foldable_group = SubResource("FoldableGroup_tvbkj")

[node name="RichTextLabel" type="RichTextLabel" parent="DockTabContainer/HelpTab/GettingStarted/VBoxContainer/ConcurrenciesHelp" unique_id=1890232147]
visible = false
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(560, 0)
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
size_flags_vertical = 3
theme_override_styles/normal = SubResource("StyleBoxEmpty_2vjd2")
theme_override_styles/focus = SubResource("StyleBoxEmpty_2vjd2")
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "When running multiple instances of your project, as is the case with multiplayer games where two or more instances is run for debugging. The two instances will log into the same file, and by default. Entries are tagged with a unique instance ID to help distinguish which instance logged what entry. The instance ID can be removed by erasing the {instance_id} tag from the [color=fc4674]Entry Format[/color] setting.

To see the ID of an instance, use the [color=fc4674]Display Instance ID[/color] hotkey([i]Ctrl + Shift + I[/i] by default). This will display the instance ID on your screen in your game. Within the Settings tab of the dock, under ID Overlay, you'll find settings to customize it's behavior and how it's displayed. Including the font used, size, outline and color to suit your game's resolution and ensure it is clearly visible. "
fit_content = true

