[node name="RichTextLabel" type="RichTextLabel" parent="DockTabContainer/HelpTab/Methods/VBoxContainer/FunctionsHelp" unique_id=208538217]
visible = false
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
size_flags_vertical = 3
theme_override_styles/normal = SubResource("StyleBoxEmpty_2vjd2")
theme_override_styles/focus = SubResource("StyleBoxEmpty_2vjd2")
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "[font_size=14]All methods are accessible using the [color=violet]Log[color=white] autoload.
Hotkeys can be customized by navigating to [color=darkgray][i]res://addons/GDLogger/[/i][color=white], where the shortcut resources are located.


[color=#dcdcaa]Log[/color].[color=#6dc2ff]start_session[/color]()
    Starts a logging session, creating new .log files and enabling entry logging.
    [color=#6a9955][i]Hotkey: Ctrl + Shift + O[/i][/color]

[color=#dcdcaa]Log[/color].[color=#6dc2ff]msg[/color]([color=#c586c0]log_msg[/color]: [color=#4ec9b0]String[/color], [color=#c586c0]category_name[/color]: [color=#c586c0]int[/color] = [color=#b5cea8]0[/color], [color=#c586c0]print_msg[/color]: [color=#4ec9b0]bool[/color] = [color=#569cd6]false[/color])
    Logs an entry into the specified [i]category_index[/i]. You can optionally print any entry to the output as well using [i]print_msg[/i].
    Example:
        [color=#dcdcaa]Log[/color].[color=#6dc2ff]entry[/color]([color=#ce9178]\"Player's current health: \"[/color] + [color=#dcdcaa]str[/color]([color=#c586c0]current_health[/color]) + [color=#ce9178]\" / \"[/color] + [color=#dcdcaa]str[/color]([color=#c586c0]max_health[/color]), [color=#b5cea8]1[/color])

[color=#dcdcaa]Log[/color].[color=#6dc2ff]stop_session[/color]()
    Stops the active logging session.
    [color=#6a9955][i]Hotkey: Ctrl + Shift + P[/i][/color]


There are two signals available to help you synchronize the plugin with game logic.[color=palegolderod]
	session_toggled([i]toggled_on: bool[/i])
	msg_logged([i]category_name: String, msg: String[/i])"
fit_content = true

[node name="HotkeysHelp" type="FoldableContainer" parent="DockTabContainer/HelpTab/Methods/VBoxContainer" unique_id=664124483]
unique_name_in_owner = true
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
theme = ExtResource("4_o07th")
folded = true
title = "Hotkeys"
foldable_group = SubResource("FoldableGroup_fx5fv")

[node name="RichTextLabel" type="RichTextLabel" parent="DockTabContainer/HelpTab/Methods/VBoxContainer/HotkeysHelp" unique_id=1418471264]
visible = false
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
size_flags_vertical = 3
theme_override_styles/normal = SubResource("StyleBoxEmpty_2vjd2")
theme_override_styles/focus = SubResource("StyleBoxEmpty_2vjd2")
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "There are four hotkeys available to interact with GDLogger during runtime. 
[b]Start Session[/b][/color][color=#d4d4d4]:[/color]           [color=#6a9955]Ctrl[/color] + [color=#6a9955]Shift[/color] + [color=#dcdcaa]O[/color]
[b]Stop Session[/b][/color][color=#d4d4d4]:[/color]            [color=#6a9955]Ctrl[/color] + [color=#6a9955]Shift[/color] + [color=#dcdcaa]P[/color]
[b]Display Instance ID[/b][/color][color=#d4d4d4]:[/color]  [color=#6a9955]Ctrl[/color] + [color=#6a9955]Shift[/color] + [color=#dcdcaa]I[/color]
Hotkeys can be changed using InputEventShortcut resources. As such, they're excluded and doesn't crowd your InputMap. You can easily add, change or remove bindings to the resources in the Settings tab which opens the resources in the Inspector."
fit_content = true

[node name="FileLimitsHelp" type="FoldableContainer" parent="DockTabContainer/HelpTab/Methods/VBoxContainer" unique_id=1580460435]
unique_name_in_owner = true
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
theme = ExtResource("4_o07th")
folded = true
title = "File Limits"
foldable_group = SubResource("FoldableGroup_fx5fv")

[node name="RichTextLabel" type="RichTextLabel" parent="DockTabContainer/HelpTab/Methods/VBoxContainer/FileLimitsHelp" unique_id=1956207480]
visible = false
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
size_flags_vertical = 3
theme_override_styles/normal = SubResource("StyleBoxEmpty_2vjd2")
theme_override_styles/focus = SubResource("StyleBoxEmpty_2vjd2")
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "[font_size=14]While log files are lightweight, creating an unlimited number of files or logging for extended periods is never recommended. GDLogger features limitations to control log file lengths. These limitations can be disabled if necessary, but doing so may affect performance. If you experience micro-stuttering or other issues, enable these settings or lower their limits.

[font_size=14]File Count:[font_size=14]
This option defines the maximum number of .log files allowed in each category folder. The default limit is 10. When the limit is reached, the oldest file is replaced with a new one. Only [i].log[/i] files that haven't been renamed are subject to the file count handling,

[color=darkgray][i]Recommended:[/i][/color]
[i]A file count limit of 10–20 is suitable for most use cases, though higher values are also supported. Setting it to 0 will disable the limitation but it's not recommended.[/i]


[font_size=14][b]Entry count[/b][font_size=14]
	As new entries are logged, they are counted, and once the limit is reached, one of the following actions is triggered:

		Overwrite Entries – Replaces the oldest entries as new ones are added.
		Restart Session – Ends the current session and starts a new one, creating a new .log file.
		Stop Session – Stops logging entirely. The session must be manually restarted using hotkeys or code.


[font_size=14][b]Session timer:[/b][font_size=14]
	Starts a timer at the beginning of a session and runs for the duration specified in the Session Duration setting. This method is useful for time-based testing. 
	The Session Timer emits the signals [color=turquoise]session_started[/color] and [color=turquoise]session_stopped[/color], which can be used to synchronize with other systems or features.
	
		Restart Session – Ends the current session and starts a new one, creating a new .log file.
		Stop Session – Stops logging entirely. The session must be manually restarted using hotkeys or code.



[b]Recommended overall settings:[/b]
Using the Entry Count method with the Overwrite Entries action provides the most consistent performance but may overwrite older data if logging continues for long periods. Familiarize yourself with the session hotkeys for manual control when needed."
fit_content = true

[node name="FormattingHelp" type="FoldableContainer" parent="DockTabContainer/HelpTab/Methods/VBoxContainer" unique_id=1185594613]
unique_name_in_owner = true
layout_mode = 2
